+# Aegis A2A Protocol — Complete Implementation (scaffold)
+
+This folder provides a multi-layer Agent-to-Agent (A2A) protocol implementation in three flavors:
+
+1) Minimal A2A scaffold:
+   - a2a/registry/service.py : Agent registry + discovery
+   - a2a/envelope/envelope.py : Signed message envelope helpers (Vault transit signing)
+   - a2a/transport/kafka_client.py : Kafka topic conventions & produce/consume helpers
+   - a2a/handshake/handshake.py : Handshake flow to exchange manifests and register peers
+   - a2a/json_schemas : JSON Schema for manifests/envelopes
+
+2) Full synchronous/asynchronous A2A:
+   - a2a/grpc/a2a.proto : gRPC definitions
+   - a2a/grpc/server.py : gRPC server (receives signed envelopes and routes them)
+   - a2a/grpc/client.py : gRPC client (sends signed envelopes)
+   - a2a/transport/kafka_client.py : asynchronous fallback / pubsub
+   - a2a/scripts/vault_issue_agent_cert.sh : helper to obtain Vault-issued certs for mTLS
+
+3) Lightweight interoperability & middleware:
+   - a2a/middleware/fastapi_dependency.py : verify envelope & call Safety Kernel for incoming plans
+   - a2a/middleware/jsonld_middleware.py : schema enforcement middleware
+   - a2a/examples/agent_integration.py : end-to-end example using handshake, gRPC & Kafka
+
+Notes & integration points:
+- Identity & Signing: envelope.sign uses Vault transit. In production verify signatures against Vault public key and Rekor entries.
+- Transport: use Kafka for async messages, gRPC/HTTPS for synchronous calls. Topic naming convention: aegis.a2a.<from>.<to>.<type>
+- Registry: registry/service.py is the canonical capability store for agents.
+- Safety: the middleware calls Safety Kernel (pre_check). Agents must not execute remote plans without passing local safety checks.
+- mTLS: use vault_issue_agent_cert.sh to request certificates from Vault PKI. Configure gRPC servers and clients to use these certs.
+
+Next steps to productionize:
+- Harden verify_envelope_signature to cryptographically validate signatures.
+- Implement Rekor-backed attestation linking for every critical action across agents.
+- Add agent authentication & admission: mutual TLS and policies stored in OPA.
+- Add persistent transaction coordinator for distributed transactions and compensating actions.
+
